      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL The cDNA encoding the iron-dependent superoxide dismutase (SOD) FSD3 has been isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. FSD3 belongs to a small gene family in Arabidopsis with at least three iron-dependent SOD&apos;s. The FSD3 gene was the SOD that was lowest expressed in rosette leaves under standard 16-h-photoperiod growth conditions |CITS: [9765550]|.</Comment>
