    <DataNode elementId="AT2G28190-MONOMER" textLabel="Superoxide dismutase [Cu-Zn] 2, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT2G28190.1" dataSource="TAIR gene name" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL The cDNA encoding the copper/zinc -dependent superoxide dismutase (SOD) CSD2 has been isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. CSD2 belongs to a small gene family in Arabidopsis with at least three copper/zinc-dependent SOD&apos;s. Its molecular function (Cu/Zn-dependent SOD) could be confirmed in a non-denaturative PAGE assay and assigned to CSD2 by immunodetection of the corresponding antiserum. The CSD2 gene showed the highest expression in rosette leaves under standard 16-h-photoperiod growth conditions |CITS: [9765550]| and increased upon salicylic acid analogs |CITS: [10550898]|. It was discussed that CSD2 contributes to the adaptation to long-term changes in photoproduced reactive oxygen species (ROS). It has been demonstrated that a copper-chaperone (AtCCS, At1g12520) is crucial for the activation of all three Cu/Zn-dependent SOD&apos;s in Arabdiopsis |CITS: [16126858]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G28190-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G28190.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAD10208" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Copper/zinc superoxide dismutase 2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-13458" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G28190.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
