    <DataNode elementId="AT3G10920-MONOMER" textLabel="manganese superoxide dismutase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G10920.1" dataSource="TAIR gene name" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="575" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL The cDNA encoding the mangan-dependent superoxide dismutase (SOD) MSD1 has been isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. MSD1 belongs to a small gene family in Arabidopsis with at least seven SOD&apos;s. Its molecular function (Mn-dependent SOD) could be confirmed in a non-denaturative PAGE assay and assigned to MSD1 by immunodetection of the corresponding antiserum. The MSD1 gene was expressed in rosette leaves under standard 16-h-photoperiod growth conditions but was otherwise unresponsive to all environmental stimuli tested |CITS: [9765550]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G10920-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G10920.1" />
